  "info": {
    "description": "Turn your documents into a searchable knowledge base. Push documents in,\nand we chunk, embed and index them; search them with one call. Access\ncontrol runs inside the search, so a caller only sees what its credential\nmay read. Use it to add retrieval to your own product or to feed an agent,\nwithout running search infrastructure yourself. One deployment serves one\ntenant, over API-key auth.\n\n### Quickstart\n\nEvery call carries `Authorization: Bearer <your API key>`. Mutating calls\nalso carry an `Idempotency-Key` you choose, so a retry is always safe.\n\n**1. Declare a schema**: the custom fields your documents carry, and which\nof them a query may filter on.\n\n```\nPOST /v1/schemas\n{ \"key\": \"invoices\",\n  \"metadata_spec\": { \"fields\": [\n    { \"name\": \"year\", \"type\": \"number\", \"filterable\": true },\n    { \"name\": \"client\", \"type\": \"keyword\", \"filterable\": true } ] } }\n```\n\n**2. Create a collection** in that schema, and say who may read it.\n\n```\nPOST /v1/collections\n{ \"key\": \"firm-1234-invoices\", \"schema_key\": \"invoices\",\n  \"visibility\": \"restricted\", \"principals\": [\"mk:firm:1234\"] }\n```\n\n**3. Push documents** as a job. Inline `text` starts at once. For files,\nsend `size` and `sha256`, `PUT` the bytes to each URL in the job's\n`uploads`, then `POST /v1/jobs/{job_id}/commit`.\n\n```\nPOST /v1/jobs\n{ \"collection_key\": \"firm-1234-invoices\",\n  \"documents\": [\n    { \"source_id\": \"inv-2024-001\", \"filename\": \"inv-2024-001.txt\",\n      \"text\": \"Invoice 2024-001 ...\",\n      \"metadata\": { \"year\": 2024, \"client\": \"acme\" } } ] }\n\nGET /v1/jobs/{job_id}    until status is SUCCEEDED, COMPLETED_WITH_ERRORS or FAILED\n```\n\nSUCCEEDED means searchable: the vector index has caught up, so a query issued\nafter it sees the document.\n\n**4. Search.** Each hit is one chunk with its `source_id`, `score`,\n`content` and metadata. Tune with `alpha` (1.0 vector, 0.0 keyword) and\n`rerank: true`.\n\n```\nPOST /v1/query\n{ \"query\": \"what did we invoice acme for in 2024\",\n  \"collection_keys\": [\"firm-1234-invoices\"],\n  \"filter\": { \"year\": 2024 }, \"top_k\": 5 }\n```\n\n**5. Delete** one document or a whole collection; both answer with a job.\n\n```\nDELETE /v1/collections/{collection_key}/documents/{source_id}\nDELETE /v1/collections/{collection_key}\n```\n\n### Principals\n\nA principal names who may read something: `source:kind:external_id`, such\nas `mk:firm:1234`. You choose the strings; they are compared verbatim.\n\n### Paging through lists\n\nList endpoints take `limit` (default 50, at most 200) and return `data`\nwith `next_cursor`. Call once without a cursor; while `next_cursor` is not\nnull, call again with `cursor=<next_cursor>`. Cursors are opaque: pass them\nback unchanged.\n\n### Errors\n\nEvery refusal is an `application/problem+json` document with a stable\n`code`. One code always arrives at one status, so branch on `code` and\nnever on `title` or `detail`.",
    "title": "soev API",
    "version": "0.29.0"
  },
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "paths": {
    "/v1/bug-reports": {
      "post": {
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/BugReportResult"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Successful Response"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/feedback": {
      "get": {
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/FeedbackPage"
                }
              },
              "text/csv": {
                "schema": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              }
            },
            "description": "Success; current authority checked before release",
            "headers": {
              "Cache-Control": {
                "schema": {
                  "const": "private, no-store",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              },
              "Vary": {
                "schema": {
                  "const": "Authorization, Cookie",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
